  "reply_text": "*One merge-blocking finding* in `leaderboard-sort` (`17941bc`) vs `main`.\n\n*High — score precision breaks ranking* · `src/rank.js:3`\n`b.score - a.score` implicitly converts decimal strings to JavaScript Numbers, violating the existing arbitrary-precision score contract. Distinct scores above 2^53 can compare as equal.\n\nVerified with lower score `\"9007199254740992\"` followed by higher score `\"9007199254740993\"`: `rankings()` incorrectly puts the lower score first, and `topN(entries, 1)` returns the wrong winner.\n\n*Recommended fix:* use the existing `compareScore(b.score, a.score)` from `src/score.js`. Add regression tests for both ranking and top-N using those values in lower-first input order.\n\nAll 3 existing tests pass; `test/rank.test.js` only exercises small scores, so it misses this. No other findings. No code changed.",
